<details class="how"><summary>How it works</summary>
<h4>Ports</h4>
<p>Every packet has a destination <b>port</b>, a number saying which service on the machine it wants. <b>443</b> is secure web traffic (HTTPS). <b>53</b> is DNS. <b>22</b> is SSH, a way to log in to a machine remotely.</p>
<h4>What a firewall does</h4>
<p>A firewall is a gatekeeper with a list of rules. Each rule says allow or block, based on things like the port, the address and which direction the traffic is going. Good firewalls start with <b>block everything</b> and then allow only what’s needed. This game starts the other way round, with everything allowed, so you have to block the bad stuff.</p>
<h4>Why block SSH and the rest</h4>
<p>If nobody outside needs to log in remotely, an open SSH port just invites strangers to keep guessing passwords. That’s called brute-forcing. The flood stands for junk sent to random ports to waste a machine’s time or find something open.</p>
<h4>Remembering conversations</h4>
<p>Most firewalls are <b>stateful</b>: they remember connections that your side started, so the replies are let back in automatically. Only unrequested traffic from outside gets checked against the rules.</p>
<h4>The game</h4>
<p>Let customers in (HTTPS and DNS) and keep the attacks out. Each breach costs a life. Blocking a customer’s port turns them away, which the scoreboard counts too.</p>
</details>

<div class="cx word"><span class="lb" style="background:#fff">Word origin</span><div class="big">firewall<i>(n.)</i></div><p>Named after the walls built between buildings to stop a fire spreading from one to the next. Same job, different kind of fire.</p></div>
<h3 class="big" style="margin-top:88px;max-width:22ch">How one attacker borrows a crowd of gadgets</h3>
<p class="intro">Cameras, routers and TVs get hacked, then wait for an order. When it comes, they all knock on the same website at once. Pick how many, and see where it breaks.</p>
<div class="stage">
<div class="bar">
<label>Bots in the botnet: <b id="dd-n">100</b><input id="dd-s" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="40" aria-label="Number of bots"></label>
